{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1060659-cuckoo-clock-fetish-for-kinfolk","id":1060659,"title":"Cuckoo Clock Fetish for Kinfolk","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-09T14:14:12-08:00","id":1060659,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Cuckoo Clock Fetish for Kinfolk","content":"So I have this idea for a Get of Fenris Fetish, but I got questions. It's a traditional <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuckoo_clock#First_cuckoo_clocks_made_in_the_Black_Forest\" target=\"_blank\">Black Forest Cockoo Clock</a> designed as a warning system for kinfolk. I am not sure how feasible this fetish is. Most fetish seem to be tools a Garou or kin keep on their person. This clock is designed for a location.<br /> <br /> My ideas are in flux right now, but here is what I have: Basically, a Garou donates gnosis to wind the clock. These would be Kinfolk a Garou has a close relationship with and visits on a regular basis (Weekly, maybe monthly). The clock ticks when charged with Gnosis and will sound at certain stimulus instead of at the hour.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what the stimulus would be. If a Bane is in the area or a Kinhawk, but I don't think that would be too useful to kinfolk. Or perhaps the clock will sound and the spirit in the clock will send a message to the Garou the fetish belongs to? Or perhaps the Garou can send a spirit messenger to sound the clock in case of Danger?<br /> <br /> Also, what would the point value be for a fetish such as this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 03-09-2017, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T20:30:57-08:00","id":1060742,"title":"","content":"Sounds better as a talen imo, however depending on where the kin folk lives a bane alarm might be triggered a bit to much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T23:25:58-08:00","id":1060770,"title":"","content":"Like the Weasley clock in Harry Potter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T06:56:05-08:00","id":1060855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1060659-cuckoo-clock-fetish-for-kinfolk?p=1060770#post1060770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like the Weasley clock in Harry Potter?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Similar concept, but less individualized to specific people. I was planning on having the Fetish/Talon be an heirloom pasted down though the generations. To your average person, it looks like your average cockoo clock. <br /> <br /> Though, apparently I am confused on the difference between a Fetish and a Talon? I thought Talons were more one time use items?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T08:40:52-08:00","id":1060895,"title":"","content":"I introduced a similar fetish into a game before, less classic more modern though. I had a Glasswalker character who wore a smart watch (like those ones that monitor your heart beat) that would go off when something dangerous was about to happen (like the danger sense gift). It didn't tell him what the danger was just that it was imminent.<br /> <br /> Talons are one time use items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T10:32:18-08:00","id":1060927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1060659-cuckoo-clock-fetish-for-kinfolk#post1060659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have this idea for a Get of Fenris Fetish, but I got questions. It's a traditional <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuckoo_clock#First_cuckoo_clocks_made_in_the_Black_Forest\" target=\"_blank\">Black Forest Cockoo Clock</a> designed as a warning system for kinfolk. I am not sure how feasible this fetish is. Most fetish seem to be tools a Garou or kin keep on their person. This clock is designed for a location.<br /> <br /> My ideas are in flux right now, but here is what I have: Basically, a Garou donates gnosis to wind the clock. These would be Kinfolk a Garou has a close relationship with and visits on a regular basis (Weekly, maybe monthly). The clock ticks when charged with Gnosis and will sound at certain stimulus instead of at the hour.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what the stimulus would be. If a Bane is in the area or a Kinhawk, but I don't think that would be too useful to kinfolk. Or perhaps the clock will sound and the spirit in the clock will send a message to the Garou the fetish belongs to? Or perhaps the Garou can send a spirit messenger to sound the clock in case of Danger?<br /> <br /> Also, what would the point value be for a fetish such as this?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can have it specifically be a Kin Fetish so it can be activated by the Kinfolk in the home. Wind I once a day to activate it. Have it alarm when Wyrm taint (per the Sense Wyrm Gift) enters the home.<br /> Level 2-3, Gnosis 5. It's a relatively simple.<br /> <br /> If you want to get more complex than that, then you would up the level and Gnosis based on additional effects it might have.<br /> <br /> And like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1619_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1619\" data-vbnamecard=\"1619\">Derzhuzad</a> said, Talens are 1 shot items. Fetishes function whenever activated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}